#: apps/seo/data.py:23
msgid "Pay your way"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:24
msgid "Buy an eSIM with crypto"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:25
#, python-format
msgid "Buy an eSIM with crypto — no account, no KYC, from just $%(price)s"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:27
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Pay for a travel eSIM with Bitcoin, USDT, Ether and more. No account, no "
"KYC, QR code delivered as soon as the payment confirms. Plans from $"
"%(price)s."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:31
msgid ""
"We take cryptocurrency for mobile data, which most eSIM sellers still do "
"not. Choose a plan, pick crypto at checkout, send the amount shown on "
"screen, and the QR code is in your inbox as soon as the network confirms the "
"payment."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:36
msgid "What you can pay with"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:37
msgid ""
"Crypto checkout runs through our payment processor, which handles the major "
"coins and stablecoins: Bitcoin, Ether, Tether, USD Coin, Litecoin, TRON, "
"BNB, Solana and a long tail of others. The live list, the exact network and "
"the exact amount all appear on the payment screen before you move anything, "
"so nothing rests on you guessing which asset we support this week."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:42
msgid ""
"Plans are priced in US dollars. The crypto amount is worked out from the "
"rate at the moment the payment screen opens and is held for a short window, "
"which is the one good reason to send straight away rather than an hour later."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:46
msgid "No account, no passport, no KYC"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:47
msgid ""
"Buying a week of mobile data should not require an identity file. There is "
"no account to create, no document to upload and no verification queue. We "
"ask for an email address so the QR code has somewhere to land, and that is "
"the whole of it."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:50
msgid ""
"If you would rather not give out your usual address, an alias or forwarding "
"address works perfectly well. The eSIM is tied to the profile on your "
"handset, not to a name on a form."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:54
msgid "How delivery works after you send"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:55
msgid ""
"The order page watches for the payment and updates itself. When the "
"transaction confirms, the QR code appears there and the same code goes out "
"by email, so you have it in two places before you close the laptop."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:58
msgid ""
"Install the profile at home on Wi-Fi. The plan does not start counting until "
"the eSIM first connects to a network at your destination, so an early "
"install costs you nothing."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:62
msgid "If something goes wrong"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:63
msgid ""
"Crypto payments are one-way, so we would rather sort out a problem than "
"argue about it. If you underpaid, overpaid, sent late or sent on an "
"unexpected network, write to support with the transaction hash and the order "
"reference and we will fix the order by hand."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:70
msgid "No identity checks"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:71
msgid ""
"No account, no passport upload, no selfie. An email address and a payment is "
"the entire purchase flow."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:73
msgid "Delivered in minutes"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:74
msgid ""
"The QR code is released automatically the moment the transaction confirms, "
"day or night, with nobody in the loop."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:76
msgid "Same price as paying by card"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:77
msgid ""
"We do not add a surcharge for paying in crypto. The only extra is the "
"network fee your own wallet charges to broadcast the transaction."
msgstr ""

