msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:85
msgid "Do I need an account to pay with crypto?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:86
msgid ""
"No. Checkout takes an email address and a payment. You can create an account "
"later if you want your eSIMs and top-ups in one place, but nothing forces "
"you to."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:88
msgid "How long does confirmation take?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:89
msgid ""
"Usually a few minutes. It depends on the coin and how busy its network is: a "
"stablecoin transfer on a fast chain clears almost immediately, an on-chain "
"Bitcoin payment waits for a block. The order page updates by itself, so you "
"can leave it open."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:92
msgid "What happens if the rate moves while I am paying?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:93
msgid ""
"The quoted amount is locked for a short window at the payment screen. If it "
"expires before you send, the processor will show you a fresh quote rather "
"than quietly accepting the wrong amount."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:96
msgid "Can I get a refund to my wallet?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:97
msgid ""
"Yes. An unused eSIM that has not been installed is refundable within 24 "
"hours of purchase, and we refund crypto payments to a wallet address you "
"give us."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:99
msgid "Is paying in crypto anonymous?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:100
msgid ""
"It is private, not anonymous. We never ask for identity documents and we do "
"not know who you are, but a blockchain transaction is public by design and "
"your email address is attached to the order so we can support it."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:106
msgid "Bitcoin"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:108
msgid "BTC accepted"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:109
msgid "Buy an eSIM with Bitcoin"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:110
#, python-format
msgid "Buy an eSIM with Bitcoin — travel data from just $%(price)s"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:112
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Pay for a travel eSIM in BTC. No account, no KYC, QR code delivered as soon "
"as the transaction confirms. Data plans in %(count)s destinations from $"
"%(price)s."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:116
msgid ""
"Bitcoin buys mobile data here. Pick a destination, choose Bitcoin at "
"checkout, send the amount to the address on screen, and the eSIM lands in "
"your inbox as soon as the transaction confirms."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:121
msgid "Why pay for travel data in BTC"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:122
msgid ""
"A card issued at home is a nuisance abroad. Banks flag foreign merchants, "
"three-digit security steps arrive by SMS to a number you cannot receive on, "
"and the whole thing fails at the exact moment you have no data to sort it "
"out. A Bitcoin payment has none of those failure modes: your wallet does not "
"care which country you are standing in."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:127
msgid ""
"It is also the honest option for anyone who simply prefers not to hand a "
"card number to another website. We never see one either way, but with BTC "
"there is nothing to see in the first place."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:131
msgid "Confirmations, fees and how long it takes"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:132
msgid ""
"An on-chain Bitcoin payment is not instant. We wait for network confirmation "
"before releasing the eSIM, which on a quiet day is a matter of minutes and "
"on a congested day is longer. Set a normal fee rather than the cheapest one "
"your wallet offers, or the transaction will sit in the queue while you sit "
"at the gate."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:136
msgid ""
"The network fee goes to miners, not to us. We do not add anything on top of "
"the dollar price for paying this way."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:139
msgid "The amount is quoted and held"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:140
msgid ""
"Plans are priced in US dollars, so the payment screen converts to BTC at the "
"rate at that moment and holds the quote for a short window. Send the exact "
"amount displayed - not a rounded version of it - and the order matches "
"itself automatically."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:144
msgid ""
"If the window expires, refresh for a new quote instead of sending against "
"the old one."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:147
msgid "What you do not need"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:148
msgid ""
"No account. No passport. No proof of address. No app to install before you "
"can even see a price. You need an email address for the QR code and a phone "
"that supports eSIM."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:154
msgid "On-chain BTC"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:155
msgid ""
"Send from any wallet or exchange to the address shown. Nothing custodial, "
"nothing to sign up for."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:157
msgid "Released on confirmation"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:158
msgid ""
"The order page polls for you and hands over the QR code the moment the "
"network confirms the transaction."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:160
msgid "No card, no bank in the way"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:161
msgid ""
"No foreign-transaction block, no 3-D Secure code sent to a phone number you "
"cannot reach while abroad."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:165
msgid "Bitcoin (BTC), on-chain"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:166
msgid "Any wallet or exchange withdrawal"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:167
msgid "Exact quoted amount, held for a short window"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:170
msgid "How many confirmations do you wait for?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:171
msgid ""
"We follow the payment processor's confirmation policy for BTC, which is "
"designed to release fast without accepting an unconfirmed transaction. In "
"practice most orders complete within minutes of the transaction being "
"broadcast with a sensible fee."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:174
msgid "What if I send slightly the wrong amount?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:175
msgid ""
"Underpayments and overpayments are recoverable. Contact support with the "
"transaction hash and the order reference and we will either release the eSIM "
"or return the difference."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:178
msgid "Can I pay from an exchange account?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:179
msgid ""
"Yes, but check the withdrawal fee your exchange deducts, because it can "
"leave the received amount short of the quote. Sending from a self-custody "
"wallet avoids that."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:181
msgid "Do you accept Bitcoin for top-ups too?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:182
msgid ""
"Yes. Top-ups use the same checkout, so you can add data to an eSIM you "
"already installed and pay for it in BTC."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:187
msgid "USDT"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:189
msgid "Stablecoin accepted"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:190
msgid "Buy an eSIM with USDT"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:191
#, python-format
msgid "Buy an eSIM with USDT (Tether) — data plans from just $%(price)s"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:193
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Pay for a travel eSIM in USDT. Dollar-priced plans, no account, no KYC, "
"instant QR delivery. The checkout shows the exact network and address. From $"
"%(price)s."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:197
msgid ""
"USDT is the least dramatic way to pay for data. Plans are priced in dollars "
"and Tether is pegged to the dollar, so the number you are quoted is the "
"number you send and nothing moves underneath you while the transfer settles."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:202
msgid "Why a stablecoin is the practical choice"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:203
msgid ""
"With a volatile coin there is always a gap between the quote and the "
"confirmation, and one of the two parties carries that risk. With USDT there "
"is essentially no gap. You see a dollar price, you send a dollar-equivalent "
"amount, the order matches, the eSIM is released."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:207
msgid ""
"It also makes refunds tidy. If you cancel an unused eSIM within the refund "
"window, the amount that comes back is the amount that went out rather than "
"an argument about exchange rates."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:211
msgid "Send on the network the checkout names"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:212
msgid ""
"USDT exists on several blockchains, and a transfer sent on the wrong one is "
"slow and painful to recover. The payment screen shows the network next to "
"the address. Copy both. If your wallet asks which chain to use, use that one "
"and no other."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:215
msgid ""
"Transfer fees differ enormously between chains, so if your wallet supports "
"more than one of the networks on offer, the cheaper option is usually worth "
"taking."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:218
msgid "Delivery is automatic"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:219
msgid ""
"Stablecoin transfers confirm quickly, so the usual experience is that the "
"order page updates while you are still looking at it. The QR code appears "
"there and is emailed to you at the same time."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:222
msgid ""
"Install the profile on Wi-Fi before you travel. The plan starts on first "
"connection at your destination, not on install."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:225
msgid "No account and no verification"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:226
msgid ""
"There is no sign-up wall in front of the price, no identity check and no "
"minimum order. An email address is the only thing we need, and it exists so "
"the QR code has somewhere to go."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:232
msgid "No exchange-rate drift"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:233
msgid ""
"A dollar-pegged token against a dollar price means the quote and the "
"settlement agree with each other."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:235
msgid "Confirms quickly"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:236
msgid ""
"Most USDT transfers settle in well under a minute, so the eSIM is usually "
"released before you have switched tabs."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:238
msgid "The network is shown, not guessed"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:239
msgid ""
"Address and chain appear together at checkout, which is the single most "
"common way a stablecoin payment goes wrong elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:243
msgid "Tether (USDT) on the networks shown at checkout"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:244
msgid "USD Coin (USDC) as an alternative stablecoin"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:245
msgid "Exact amount and network displayed before you send"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:248
msgid "Which USDT network should I use?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:249
msgid ""
"Whichever one the payment screen displays for your order. It names the chain "
"next to the deposit address, and sending on a different chain is the one "
"mistake that needs manual recovery."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:252
msgid "Is the price the same as paying by card?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:253
msgid ""
"Yes. The dollar amount does not change with the payment method. You pay the "
"network transfer fee your wallet charges, and nothing to us."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:255
msgid "How fast is the eSIM delivered?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:256
msgid ""
"As soon as the transfer confirms, which for USDT is normally a matter of "
"seconds to a couple of minutes. The QR code appears on the order page and in "
"your email."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:258
msgid "Can I pay with USDC instead?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:259
msgid ""
"Yes. USDC and the other major stablecoins appear in the same checkout, and "
"everything on this page applies to them in the same way."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:264 templates/orders/checkout.html:66
msgid "Card"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:266
msgid "Cards and wallets"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:267
msgid "Buy an eSIM with a card"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:268
#, python-format
msgid "Buy an eSIM with a card — Visa, Mastercard, Amex, from just $%(price)s"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:270
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Pay for a travel eSIM by card: Visa, Mastercard and Amex through Stripe, "
"plus Apple Pay and Google Pay. No account, no subscription. From $%(price)s."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:274
msgid ""
"Cards work the way you would expect and nothing clever happens. Stripe runs "
"the checkout, we never see the card number, and the QR code is on screen "
"before you have put your wallet away."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:279
msgid "What we accept"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:280
msgid ""
"Visa, Mastercard and American Express, along with the wallets your device "
"offers - Apple Pay and Google Pay appear automatically when your browser and "
"phone support them, which saves typing a card number on a hotel Wi-Fi "
"connection."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:283
msgid ""
"Everything is charged in US dollars. If your account is held in another "
"currency, your bank converts at its own rate, and a card with no foreign-"
"transaction fee is worth using here as everywhere else."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:287
msgid "Your card details never reach our servers"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:288
msgid ""
"Payment pages are hosted by Stripe. The card number goes from your browser "
"to them, and what comes back to us is a yes or a no plus the last four "
"digits for your receipt. There is no card data on our side to leak."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:291
msgid ""
"Your bank may add a 3-D Secure step, which is the one-tap approval in your "
"banking app. It is normal and it is not us asking for anything extra."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:294
msgid "One payment, not a subscription"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:295
msgid ""
"A plan is a single purchase. Nothing renews by itself, there is no "
"membership fee and there is no stored card quietly charging you next month. "
"When you need more data you buy a top-up on purpose, and it goes onto the "
"eSIM you already have."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:298
msgid ""
"If you specifically want a plan that renews, that is a separate, clearly "
"labelled choice - never the default hidden under a price."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:301
msgid "If your card is declined"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:302
msgid ""
"Foreign merchants get flagged, particularly on the first attempt from an "
"unusual location. Approve the transaction in your banking app and try again, "
"or switch to another card. Crypto checkout is there as a fallback when a "
"bank will not cooperate and your flight will not wait."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:309
msgid "Visa, Mastercard, Amex"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:310
msgid ""
"Plus Apple Pay and Google Pay where your device supports them, with no extra "
"fee from us for any of them."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:312
msgid "Hosted by Stripe"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:313
msgid ""
"PCI handling stays with the payment processor. We store an order and an "
"email address, never a card number."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:315
msgid "No auto-renew by default"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:316
msgid ""
"One plan, one charge. Top-ups are deliberate purchases, not a standing order."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:319
msgid "Visa"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:319
msgid "Mastercard"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:319
msgid "American Express"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:319
msgid "Apple Pay"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:319
msgid "Google Pay"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:322
msgid "Do I need an account to pay by card?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:323
msgid ""
"No. Guest checkout takes an email address and a card. An account is optional "
"and only exists to keep your eSIMs, orders and top-ups together."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:325
msgid "Which currency am I charged in?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:326
msgid ""
"US dollars. Your bank converts to your home currency at its own rate if your "
"account is held in something else."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:328
msgid "Will anything renew automatically?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:329
msgid ""
"Not unless you deliberately choose a renewing plan. A standard data plan is "
"a one-off purchase and expires on its own."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:331
msgid "Is my card stored?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:332
msgid ""
"Not by us. Stripe handles the payment and we keep only the order record and "
"the last four digits shown on your receipt."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:334
msgid "My bank keeps declining the payment. What now?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:335
msgid ""
"Approve it in your banking app if it asks, then retry. If the bank will not "
"budge, crypto checkout takes about a minute and needs no bank at all."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:356
msgid "Price per GB and per day"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:357
msgid ""
"Printed on every plan, next to the price. You never have to divide anything "
"yourself."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:358
msgid ""
"Look for a per-GB figure on the plan list. If it is missing, divide the "
"price by the gigabytes before you compare."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:360
msgid "Account needed to buy"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:361
msgid ""
"No. Checkout takes an email address and a payment, and an account is "
"optional afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:362
msgid ""
"Try reaching their checkout without creating an account or installing an app "
"first."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:363 apps/seo/data.py:516
msgid "Crypto accepted"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:364
msgid "Yes. Bitcoin, USDT, Ether and other major coins, with no surcharge."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:365
msgid "Check the payment options at their checkout, not the marketing page."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:366
msgid "Subscription or auto-renew"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:367
msgid "Never by default. A plan is a one-off purchase that expires on its own."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:368
msgid ""
"Read the small print under the price for renewal wording and stored-card "
"terms."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:369
msgid "Delivery"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:370
msgid ""
"QR code on the confirmation page and by email the moment payment clears, "
"plus a one-tap install link on iPhone."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:372
msgid ""
"Check whether the profile is delivered inside an app only, and what happens "
"if you lose the phone it was installed on."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:374
msgid "Top-ups"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:375
msgid ""
"Added to the eSIM you already installed. No second QR code, no second "
"profile."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:376
msgid "Check whether more data means a brand new profile to install."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:377
msgid "Refund before install"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:378
msgid "Unused, uninstalled eSIMs are refunded within 24 hours of purchase."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:379
msgid "Find the refund window and the exact wording that voids it."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:380
msgid "Coverage on one plan"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:381
msgid ""
"Single-country plans plus regional plans covering whole continents, all "
"listed publicly with their prices."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:383
msgid ""
"Compare like for like: same destination, same gigabytes, same number of days."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:389
msgid ""
"one of the best known travel eSIM apps, and for many travellers the first "
"eSIM they ever installed"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:392
msgid ""
"If you have heard of travel eSIMs at all, you have probably heard of Airalo. "
"It is a large, app-first marketplace with a wide catalogue. We are a website "
"that sells the same kind of thing without the app, without the account and "
"without the advertising budget baked into the price."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:398
msgid ""
"The structural difference is distribution. An app-first business has to buy "
"its installs, and app-install advertising is expensive, continuous and "
"ultimately paid for by whoever buys the data. We do not run app-install "
"campaigns, because there is no app to install: the site works in any browser "
"and the eSIM lives in your phone settings where it belongs."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:403
msgid ""
"The second difference is what we show you. Every plan here publishes its "
"price per gigabyte and per day next to the headline price, which makes a 3 "
"GB plan and a 5 GB plan directly comparable instead of a puzzle. Compare "
"that with whatever you are looking at and you will know within ten seconds "
"which is better value."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:409
msgid "App required"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:410
msgid ""
"No app. Buy in a browser, install the profile into your phone's own "
"settings, manage it from any device."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:412
msgid "Check whether buying, topping up and support all assume the app."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:415
msgid "Thin margin, not a marketing budget"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:416
msgid ""
"We buy wholesale and add a small margin. Nothing in your price is funding an "
"app-install campaign."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:418
msgid "Crypto at checkout"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:419
msgid ""
"Bitcoin, USDT and other major coins, which almost nobody in this category "
"accepts."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:420
msgid "Every price in public"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:421
msgid ""
"The whole catalogue, including the per-GB maths, is on the open web with no "
"download required to see it."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:425
msgid "Is this an Airalo reseller?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:426
msgid ""
"No. We are an independent seller with our own supply, our own pricing and "
"our own support. We are not affiliated with Airalo in any way."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:428
msgid "Will the coverage be the same?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:429
msgid ""
"Travel eSIMs from every seller ride on the same local networks - there are "
"only so many mobile operators in any country. Each destination page lists "
"the operators your eSIM will use, so you can check before you buy rather "
"than after."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:432
msgid "Do you have an app?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:433
msgid ""
"No, and that is deliberate. Everything runs in the browser, and the eSIM "
"itself is managed in your phone's normal mobile-data settings."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:439
msgid "a travel eSIM brand built around unlimited-data plans"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:441
msgid ""
"Holafly made its name on unlimited data. We sell unlimited plans too, but we "
"also sell sized ones, and we think the choice matters: most trips do not "
"need unlimited, and paying for it anyway is the most common way travellers "
"overspend on data."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:446
msgid ""
"Unlimited is the right answer when you are tethering a laptop for a "
"fortnight or streaming every evening. It is the wrong answer for a long "
"weekend of maps, messaging and a couple of video calls, where a small bundle "
"costs a fraction of it. Because we publish the price per day and per "
"gigabyte on every plan, the comparison is right there and you can pick the "
"cheaper one honestly."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:451
msgid ""
"We are also plain about what unlimited means anywhere in this industry: no "
"data cap and no overage bill, but local networks do apply fair-use shaping "
"to extreme continuous use, mostly heavy tethering. Anyone telling you "
"otherwise is selling you a network they do not operate."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:457
msgid "Sized plans as well as unlimited"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:458
msgid ""
"Both. Bundles from small to large plus unlimited durations, side by side, "
"with the per-day price on each."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:460
msgid ""
"Check whether a smaller, cheaper plan is offered at all for your "
"destination, or only unlimited."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:464
msgid "Pick the size you actually need"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:465
msgid ""
"Sized bundles and unlimited plans sit next to each other, priced per day, so "
"the cheaper choice is visible."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:467
msgid "Unlimited where it earns its place"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:468
msgid ""
"Unlimited durations in a large share of destinations, for the trips that "
"genuinely warrant them."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:470
msgid "Straight talk about fair use"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:471
msgid ""
"We describe shaping honestly rather than promising something no operator "
"delivers."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:474
msgid "Do you sell unlimited data plans?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:475
msgid ""
"Yes, in a large share of destinations, for durations from about a week to a "
"month. They are listed alongside sized bundles so you can compare the daily "
"price."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:477
msgid "Is unlimited really unlimited?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:478
msgid ""
"There is no cap and no overage bill from us. Local networks apply fair-use "
"shaping to extreme continuous use, which in practice affects heavy tethering "
"rather than normal travel use. That is true of every unlimited travel eSIM, "
"whoever sells it."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:481
msgid "How do I know which is cheaper for my trip?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:482
msgid ""
"Look at the price per day on both. If your trip is short and light on data, "
"a sized bundle usually wins; if you are working off the connection for "
"weeks, unlimited usually does."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:489
msgid "a travel eSIM service from the team behind NordVPN"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:491
msgid ""
"Saily comes out of a security company, and its pitch bundles travel data "
"with security extras. Ours does not bundle anything: you are buying mobile "
"data, at the thinnest margin we can run on, and whatever else you use is "
"your business."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:496
msgid ""
"Bundles are fine when you want everything in the bundle. They are a way of "
"paying for things you do not want when you do not. If you already run a VPN, "
"or you have decided you do not need one, a data plan with nothing strapped "
"to it is simply cheaper per gigabyte, and the per-gigabyte figure is printed "
"on every plan here so you can check that claim rather than take it."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:501
msgid ""
"On privacy, the relevant fact about us is small and verifiable: we never see "
"your traffic, and we hold an email address, your orders and the usage "
"counter the network reports. There is no account required to buy in the "
"first place, which is a stronger privacy position than any feature list."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:507
msgid "Bundled extras in the price"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:508
msgid "None. You are paying for data and nothing else."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:509
msgid ""
"Work out what the bundled software is worth to you before comparing prices."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:512
msgid "Data, unbundled"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:513
msgid "No security suite folded into the price of your gigabytes."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:514
msgid "Nothing to sign up for"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:515
msgid ""
"No account is required to buy, which is the simplest privacy guarantee there "
"is."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:517
msgid ""
"Pay in Bitcoin or USDT if you would rather not attach a card to the purchase."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:520
msgid "Do you include a VPN?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:521
msgid ""
"No. We sell mobile data. If you want a VPN, choose one on its own merits "
"rather than because it came attached to a SIM."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:523
msgid "Is the connection secure without one?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:524
msgid ""
"You are on a mobile network rather than a public hotspot, and modern apps "
"and sites are encrypted end to end. A VPN changes who can see your traffic "
"metadata, which may or may not matter to you."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:527
msgid "What do you store about me?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:528
msgid ""
"An email address, your orders, and the data-usage counter the network "
"reports for your eSIM. We never see the content of your traffic."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:534
msgid "a travel eSIM seller with a wide regional catalogue"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:536
msgid ""
"Nomad and eSIMsterr are aimed at roughly the same traveller: someone "
"crossing borders who wants one profile to keep working. The differences "
"worth knowing are structural - how you pay, whether you need an account, and "
"whether the per-gigabyte price is put in front of you or left for you to "
"calculate."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:542
msgid ""
"We sell regional plans covering whole continents alongside single-country "
"plans, and both are listed publicly with the price per gigabyte and per day "
"attached. For a multi-country trip the regional plan is nearly always "
"cheaper than a handful of single-country ones, and because the numbers are "
"on the page you can prove that to yourself in a minute."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:547
msgid ""
"Payment is the other structural difference. We take cards through Stripe and "
"crypto through our processor, there is no credit balance to preload, and "
"there is no account in the way of the checkout."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:552
msgid "Credits or wallet balance"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:553
msgid "None. You pay for the plan you are buying, when you buy it."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:554
msgid ""
"Check whether you have to preload a balance, and what happens to unspent "
"credit."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:557
msgid "Regional plans that cross borders"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:558
msgid ""
"One profile for a whole continent, reconnecting to the next local network on "
"its own."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:560
msgid "The maths is done for you"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:561
msgid ""
"Price per gigabyte and per day on every plan, so comparisons take seconds."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:562
msgid "Pay once, no balance to top up"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:563
msgid "No wallet to preload and no unspent credit to lose track of."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:566
msgid "Do you sell regional plans?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:567
msgid ""
"Yes - continental and multi-country plans covering large groups of "
"destinations on a single profile, plus a global plan for long routes."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:569
msgid "Is a regional plan cheaper than several country plans?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:570
msgid ""
"For two or more countries, almost always. The regions page shows what each "
"plan covers and what it costs, so you can check against your own itinerary."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:572
msgid "Do I need to preload credit?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:573
msgid "No. Each plan is bought and paid for on its own."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:578
msgid "a travel eSIM service operated by the connectivity provider Transatel"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:580
msgid ""
"Ubigi comes from the operator side of the industry. We come from the "
"opposite direction: a shop that buys wholesale data and resells it as thinly "
"as it can, with every price and every plan visible on the open web."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:585
msgid ""
"Practically, the differences a traveller notices are about buying rather "
"than networking. There is no account here, no app, and no verification step: "
"an email address and a payment produces a QR code. Crypto is accepted "
"alongside cards. Nothing renews unless you deliberately choose it."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:589
msgid ""
"On the technical side, what you get is a standard eSIM profile installed "
"through a QR code or a one-tap link, sitting in your phone's own settings "
"next to your normal SIM. Your existing number keeps handling calls and "
"messages while the eSIM carries data."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:594
msgid "Where the profile lives"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:595
msgid ""
"A standard QR or one-tap LPA profile in your phone's own eSIM settings. No "
"app involved in installing or using it."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:597
msgid "Check whether installation, top-ups or support route through an app."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:600
msgid "Standard QR install"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:601
msgid ""
"Scan or tap once and the profile is in your phone's settings, where you can "
"manage it forever."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:603
msgid "No account required"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:604
msgid ""
"Buy as a guest. Create an account later only if you want your eSIMs in one "
"place."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:605 templates/catalog/home.html:40
msgid "Card or crypto"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:606
msgid ""
"Stripe for cards, major coins for everyone else, at the same dollar price."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:609
msgid "Will my phone work with it?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:610
msgid ""
"If it supports eSIM and is carrier-unlocked, yes. The compatible devices "
"page lists the handsets and shows how to check yours in about ten seconds."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:612
msgid "Can I keep my own number?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:613
msgid ""
"Yes. Your physical SIM is untouched, so calls, SMS and WhatsApp stay on your "
"own number while the eSIM carries data."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:615
msgid "Do I need to install anything before I travel?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:616
msgid ""
"Only the eSIM profile itself, on Wi-Fi, before you fly. No app, and the plan "
"does not start counting until it connects at your destination."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:622
msgid "a smaller travel eSIM seller"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:624
msgid ""
"With smaller sellers the questions are less about brand and more about "
"substance: what is actually in the catalogue, what happens when something "
"goes wrong, and whether the price is legible before you commit."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:629
msgid ""
"Our answer is to put everything in public. The full destination list, every "
"plan, every price, the per-gigabyte and per-day maths, the operators your "
"eSIM will use in each country and the refund terms are all on the open web, "
"with no account and no app between you and them."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:633
msgid ""
"Support is a person on email rather than a maze, refunds on uninstalled "
"eSIMs are handled within 24 hours of purchase, and top-ups go onto the "
"profile you already have instead of making you reinstall anything."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:638
msgid "Catalogue visible without signing up"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:639
msgid ""
"Every destination, plan and price is listed publicly, and the operators "
"behind each destination are named."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:641
msgid ""
"See how much of the catalogue you can inspect before being asked for an "
"email address."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:645
msgid "Nothing hidden behind a login"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:646
msgid "The whole catalogue and all its prices are indexable, public pages."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:647
msgid "Support you can reach"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:648
msgid "Email support with a real person, and a documented refund window."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:649
msgid "Top-ups, not reinstalls"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:650
msgid "More data goes onto the eSIM you already installed."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:653
msgid "How do I know the coverage is real?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:654
msgid ""
"Each destination page names the local operators the eSIM connects to, so you "
"can check them against the coverage you expect before buying."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:656
msgid "What if the eSIM does not work when I land?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:657
msgid ""
"Start with the troubleshooting page - data roaming switched off is the cause "
"more often than anything else - and contact support if that does not solve "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:659
msgid "Can I get a refund?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:660
msgid ""
"An unused, uninstalled eSIM is refundable within 24 hours of purchase. Once "
"a profile is installed and has carried data it cannot be resold, so it is "
"not refundable."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:675
msgid "travel"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:676
msgid "For holidays and short trips"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:677
msgid "eSIM for travel"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:678
#, python-format
msgid "eSIM for travel — data plans for your trip from just $%(price)s"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:680
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The travel eSIM done simply: pick your destination, install before you fly, "
"land with data already working. No roaming charges, no airport SIM queue. "
"From $%(price)s."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:684
msgid ""
"For a normal trip you need maps that load, messages that send and a boarding "
"pass that opens on the way to the gate. That is a small amount of data and "
"it should cost a small amount of money."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:691
msgid "3-5 GB for a week away"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:693
msgid "How much data a holiday actually uses"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:694
msgid ""
"Maps, messaging, a few searches and the occasional photo upload run to "
"roughly half a gigabyte a day for most people. A week of that is comfortably "
"inside 5 GB, and 3 GB is enough if you are out walking rather than "
"scrolling. Streaming video on mobile data is what changes the arithmetic, "
"and it changes it fast."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:698
msgid ""
"Buy for the trip you are taking rather than the trip you are worried about. "
"If you run out, a top-up goes onto the same eSIM in a couple of minutes, so "
"there is no reason to over-buy insurance data up front."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:702
msgid "Install before you fly"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:703
msgid ""
"Install the profile at home on Wi-Fi. The plan does not start counting until "
"the eSIM connects to a network at your destination, so an early install is "
"free and saves you fighting with airport Wi-Fi while jet-lagged."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:706
msgid ""
"Remember the one setting everyone misses: switch data roaming on for the "
"eSIM line. A travel eSIM technically roams on partner networks, so with that "
"setting off you will see signal bars and get no data."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:712
msgid "One country or many"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:713
msgid ""
"A single-country plan is cheapest if you stay put. Crossing borders, a "
"regional plan is almost always better value."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:715 apps/seo/data.py:1011
#: templates/orders/checkout.html:170 templates/partials/trust_features.html:10
msgid "Keep your own number"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:716
msgid ""
"Your physical SIM stays in the phone, so calls, SMS and WhatsApp carry on as "
"usual while the eSIM carries data."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:718
msgid "Share it"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:719
msgid ""
"Personal hotspot works, so one plan can put a laptop or a travelling "
"companion online too."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:725
msgid "How much data do I need for a week abroad?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:726
msgid ""
"Around 3-5 GB covers maps, messaging, browsing and a moderate number of "
"photos. Add more if you plan to stream video or work off the connection."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:728
msgid "When does the plan start?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:729
msgid ""
"On first connection at your destination, not when you buy or install it."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:730
msgid "Can I use it in more than one country?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:731
msgid ""
"A country plan works in that country. For a multi-country trip, buy the "
"regional plan that covers your route."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:736
msgid "business trips"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:737
msgid "For working travel"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:738
msgid "eSIM for business trips"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:739
#, python-format
msgid "eSIM for business trips — reliable data from just $%(price)s"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:741
#, python-format
msgid ""
"A business travel eSIM that works the moment you land: hotspot for the "
"laptop, calls over Teams and Zoom, an itemised receipt for expenses. Plans "
"from $%(price)s."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:745
msgid ""
"On a working trip the connection is not a convenience, it is the job. You "
"need data that is live before you clear the airport, enough of it to tether "
"a laptop, and a receipt your finance team will accept."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:752
msgid "5-10 GB for a week of meetings"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:754
msgid "Budget for the laptop, not just the phone"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:755
msgid ""
"Video calls are the expensive part. An hour of Teams or Zoom at normal "
"quality runs to roughly a gigabyte, and a tethered laptop syncing mail and "
"cloud drives adds more in the background. For a week with a few calls a day, "
"10 GB is a safer starting point than 5 GB."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:759
msgid ""
"If the trip is long or the calls are constant, an unlimited duration plan "
"removes the arithmetic entirely. The per-day price on each plan tells you at "
"what point that becomes the cheaper option."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:763
msgid "Receipts and expenses"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:764
msgid ""
"Every order produces an emailed confirmation with the amount, the "
"destination and the order reference, which is what an expenses system wants. "
"Nothing renews silently afterwards, so there is no surprise line on next "
"month's card statement to explain."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:771
msgid "Tether the laptop"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:772
msgid ""
"Personal hotspot is supported, so the eSIM covers the machine you actually "
"work on."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:773
msgid "Calls over the apps you already use"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:774
msgid ""
"Plans are data-only, which is fine: Teams, Zoom, Meet and WhatsApp all run "
"over data."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:776
msgid "Live before you leave the terminal"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:777
msgid ""
"Install on Wi-Fi at home and it connects on landing, with no kiosk queue and "
"no roaming bill to justify later."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:783
msgid "Can I tether my laptop?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:784
msgid ""
"Yes. Personal hotspot works on our plans, and it is the main reason to buy a "
"larger bundle than you think you need."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:786
msgid "Will my work calls go through?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:787
msgid ""
"Teams, Zoom, Meet, Slack and WhatsApp all run over data, so they work "
"normally. The plan does not carry traditional voice calls or SMS."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:789
msgid "Do I get an invoice for expenses?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:790
msgid ""
"You get an emailed order confirmation showing the amount, destination and "
"reference, which is what most expense systems need."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:795
msgid "digital nomads"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:796
msgid "For working anywhere"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:797
msgid "eSIM for digital nomads"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:798
#, python-format
msgid "eSIM for digital nomads — monthly data from just $%(price)s"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:800
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Month-long and unlimited eSIM plans for remote workers: tether the laptop, "
"hop borders without changing SIM, top up from anywhere. Plans from $"
"%(price)s."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:804
msgid ""
"Living out of a rucksack makes connectivity infrastructure. You want thirty-"
"day plans rather than seven-day ones, enough data to work from a balcony "
"when the cafe Wi-Fi is unusable, and no dependence on a shop in a city you "
"are leaving on Thursday."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:811
msgid "20 GB or unlimited, 30 days at a time"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:813
msgid "Why unlimited usually wins for a month"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:814
msgid ""
"A full-time remote worker on mobile data goes through a great deal more than "
"a tourist: calls, screen sharing, cloud sync and the occasional evening of "
"streaming. Once you are past roughly 20 GB in a month, the unlimited plan "
"for the same destination is often the cheaper line on the page, and every "
"plan shows its per-day price so you can check rather than guess."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:819
msgid ""
"Fair use is worth knowing about honestly: there is no cap and no overage "
"bill, but local networks shape extreme continuous use, which mostly means "
"very heavy tethering. An unlimited travel eSIM is an excellent primary "
"connection and a poor substitute for home broadband."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:824
msgid "The border-hopping problem"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:825
msgid ""
"If your month covers three countries, buying three country plans is both "
"more expensive and more admin. A regional plan keeps one profile alive "
"across the whole route and reconnects to each local network on its own."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:828
msgid ""
"Keep your home SIM in the phone for the bank codes and the two-factor "
"messages that follow you around, and let the eSIM carry the data."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:833
msgid "Unlimited by duration"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:834
msgid "Pay for days rather than gigabytes when your usage is unpredictable."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:835 apps/seo/views.py:180 templates/partials/footer.html:34
#: templates/seo/prices.html:82 templates/seo/prices.html:127
msgid "Regional plans"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:836
msgid ""
"One profile across a continent, which suits a route rather than a "
"destination."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:837
msgid "Top up from anywhere"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:838
msgid ""
"More data goes onto the eSIM you already installed, from any browser, in "
"about a minute."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:844
msgid "Are there 30-day plans?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:845
msgid ""
"Yes, in most destinations, both as large bundles and as unlimited durations."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:846
msgid "Can I keep one eSIM across several countries?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:847
msgid ""
"With a regional or global plan, yes. A single-country plan only works in its "
"own country."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:849
msgid "Can I work off it full time?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:850
msgid ""
"Plenty of people do. Budget generously for video calls and tethering, and "
"read the fair-use note on unlimited plans before you replace a fixed line "
"with one."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:855
msgid "students"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:856
msgid "For studying abroad"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:857
msgid "eSIM for students abroad"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:858
#, python-format
msgid "eSIM for students abroad — month-long data from just $%(price)s"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:860
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Land in your university city with working data. No local contract, no credit "
"check, no deposit - a month of data on your existing phone from $%(price)s."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:864
msgid ""
"Arriving for a semester is the worst possible time to have no connection: "
"you need maps to the halls, a bank appointment booked, and your parents able "
"to reach you before any of the local paperwork exists."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:871
msgid "10-20 GB for the first month"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:873
msgid "Cover the gap before the local contract"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:874
msgid ""
"Local operators generally want an address, a bank account and sometimes a "
"credit check, none of which you have in week one. A month of eSIM data "
"bridges that exactly, and it costs a fraction of roaming on your home plan "
"while you sort the rest out."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:878
msgid ""
"Keep your home SIM in the phone. Bank one-time codes and family calls keep "
"arriving on the number everyone already has for you, which matters more in "
"the first fortnight than it does later."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:882
msgid "What a student month looks like"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:883
msgid ""
"Campus and accommodation Wi-Fi will carry most of the heavy lifting, so the "
"eSIM is mainly covering travel, city time and the days the university "
"network is having a bad afternoon. Ten to twenty gigabytes is usually "
"generous for that."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:886
msgid ""
"If you are travelling at weekends, check whether a regional plan covering "
"your neighbouring countries costs less than a second country plan later."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:891
msgid "No contract, no credit check"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:892
msgid "Nothing to sign, no deposit and no local address needed."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:893
msgid "Month-long plans"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:894
msgid ""
"Thirty-day bundles that cover the settling-in period without committing you "
"to anything."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:896
msgid "Wi-Fi does the rest"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:897
msgid ""
"Campus and accommodation networks cover most of your usage, so the plan is "
"smaller than you would guess."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:903
msgid "Do I need a local bank account?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:904
msgid ""
"No. You buy with a card or crypto and the eSIM arrives by email. Local "
"contracts are what need a bank account, which is exactly the problem this "
"solves."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:906
msgid "Can my family still call me?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:907
msgid ""
"Yes. Your own SIM stays in the phone with your usual number, and the eSIM "
"only carries data."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:909
msgid "What if I stay longer than a month?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:910
msgid ""
"Top up the same eSIM for another month, or switch to a local contract once "
"you have the paperwork. Nothing here renews automatically."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:915
msgid "long stays"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:916
msgid "For a month or more"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:917
msgid "eSIM for long stays"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:918
#, python-format
msgid "eSIM for long stays — 30-day and unlimited plans from just $%(price)s"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:920
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Staying a month or more? Thirty-day and unlimited eSIM plans, topped up on "
"the same profile, with the price per day printed on every option. From $"
"%(price)s."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:924
msgid ""
"Beyond about three weeks the economics change. Daily price matters more than "
"headline price, top-ups matter more than the initial purchase, and the "
"ability to extend without reinstalling anything matters most of all."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:931
msgid "30-day plans, unlimited if you tether"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:933
msgid "Read the per-day price, not the sticker"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:934
msgid ""
"A 30-day plan that looks expensive next to a 7-day one is usually cheaper "
"per day, and the per-day figure is printed on every plan for exactly this "
"reason. Work out roughly how many days you are staying and compare that "
"column."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:937
msgid ""
"If you are tethering a laptop daily or streaming in the evenings, an "
"unlimited duration removes the need to predict anything at all."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:940
msgid "Extending without starting again"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:941
msgid ""
"Top-ups attach to the eSIM profile you already installed. You buy more days "
"or more data from any browser and the same profile keeps working, so there "
"is no second QR code and no reinstall on a phone you now depend on."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:944
msgid ""
"If the stay stretches into several months, a local contract may eventually "
"beat any travel plan. Until the paperwork is done, this keeps you online "
"without a commitment."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:950
msgid "Thirty days at a time"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:951
msgid "The standard long-stay unit, priced per day so the comparison is easy."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:952
msgid "Top up the same profile"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:953
msgid "Extending never means installing a new eSIM."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:954
msgid "Unlimited when usage is heavy"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:955
msgid ""
"Worth it once you are past roughly 20 GB a month or tethering regularly."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:960
msgid "What is the longest plan you sell?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:961
msgid ""
"Most destinations offer 30-day plans, and some go longer. You can also top "
"up to extend rather than buying a new eSIM."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:963
msgid "Does topping up need a new QR code?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:964
msgid "No. Top-ups apply to the profile already installed on your phone."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:965
msgid "Is unlimited worth it for a month?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:966
msgid ""
"If you tether or stream daily, usually yes. Compare the per-day price of the "
"unlimited plan against the sized bundle you would otherwise buy twice."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:971
msgid "backpacking"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:972
msgid "For multi-country routes"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:973
msgid "eSIM for backpacking"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:974
#, python-format
msgid "eSIM for backpacking — one plan across borders from just $%(price)s"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:976
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Backpacking across several countries? A regional eSIM keeps one profile "
"working the whole route, with no new SIM at every border. Plans from $"
"%(price)s."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:980
msgid ""
"A backpacking route is a border problem, not a country problem. Buying a "
"local SIM in each place means a queue, a language barrier and a new number "
"every few days, at exactly the moments you most need a map."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:987
msgid "A regional plan, 10 GB or more"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:989
msgid "One profile for the whole route"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:990
msgid ""
"Regional plans cover whole groups of countries on a single eSIM. You cross a "
"border, the profile reconnects to the next local network on its own, and "
"nothing on your phone needs touching. For any route with two or more "
"countries this is nearly always cheaper than a stack of single-country plans."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:994
msgid ""
"Check the coverage list on the regional page against your itinerary before "
"you buy. If one country on your route is missing, a small country plan for "
"that leg costs very little on top."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:998
msgid "Practical things that go wrong on the road"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:999
msgid ""
"Install the profile while you still have reliable Wi-Fi, not in a hostel car "
"park at midnight. Keep the QR code email, and keep your home SIM in the "
"phone so bank codes still reach you."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1002
msgid ""
"Data roaming must be switched on for the eSIM line. It is the single most "
"common reason a working eSIM appears not to work after a border crossing."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1007
msgid "Regional coverage"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1008
msgid "One plan across a continent, listed with the countries it covers."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1009
msgid "No SIM shop at every stop"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1010
msgid "Nothing to buy on arrival, nothing to swap, nothing to lose."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1012
msgid ""
"Your home SIM stays in the phone for calls, codes and everyone who already "
"knows how to reach you."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1018
msgid "Is one eSIM enough for several countries?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1019
msgid ""
"With a regional or global plan, yes. Check the covered-countries list "
"against your route before buying."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1021
msgid "What happens when I cross a border?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1022
msgid ""
"The eSIM reconnects to a local network in the new country by itself, "
"provided that country is covered by your plan."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1024
msgid "Is a regional plan cheaper than buying each country?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1025
msgid ""
"For two or more countries it almost always is. The per-day price on each "
"plan makes the comparison quick."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1037
msgid "Getting one"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1038
msgid "Downloaded over the internet in about two minutes, at any hour."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1039
msgid ""
"Bought in a shop or posted to you, in opening hours, in a country you are "
"not in yet."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1040
msgid "Where it lives"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1041
msgid "A chip soldered into the phone during manufacture."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1042
msgid "A plastic card in a tray you need a pin to open."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1043
msgid "Number of profiles"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1044
msgid ""
"Several stored at once on most modern phones, with one or two active "
"together."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1045
msgid "One per physical slot."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1046
msgid "Switching networks"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1047
msgid "A toggle in settings; no hardware involved."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1048
msgid "Swap the card, and try not to drop the small one."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1049
msgid "Travelling"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1050
msgid ""
"Add a local data profile and keep your own number on the physical SIM at the "
"same time."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1051
msgid ""
"Remove your home SIM to use a local one, and lose your number until you swap "
"back."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1052
msgid "Losing it"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1053
msgid ""
"Nothing to lose. The profile can usually be reinstalled by the seller if the "
"phone is replaced."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1055
msgid "Easy to lose, and a replacement means another trip to a shop."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1056
msgid "Security if the phone is stolen"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1057
msgid "Cannot be pulled out and put in another handset."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1058
msgid "Can be removed in seconds and used elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1059 templates/pages/devices.html:8
msgid "Compatibility"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1060
msgid "Needs a reasonably recent, carrier-unlocked phone."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1061
msgid "Works in almost anything, including very old handsets."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1065
msgid "What is an eSIM in simple terms?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1066
msgid ""
"It is a SIM card built into your phone that can be programmed over the "
"internet. Instead of collecting a piece of plastic, you scan a QR code and "
"the mobile plan downloads onto the chip that is already inside the device."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1069 templates/seo/what_is_esim.html:44
msgid "Is an eSIM the same as dual SIM?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1070
msgid ""
"They are related but not the same. Dual SIM means a phone can run two lines "
"at once; an eSIM is one way of providing one of those lines. Most modern "
"phones are dual SIM precisely because they pair a physical slot with an "
"eSIM, which is why you can keep your own number and add travel data at the "
"same time."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1074
msgid "Can I use an eSIM and a physical SIM together?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1075
msgid ""
"Yes, on any phone that supports both. Your physical SIM keeps handling "
"calls, SMS and your existing number while the eSIM carries data, and you "
"choose in settings which line is used for what."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1078
msgid "Does an eSIM replace my normal number?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1079
msgid ""
"No. A travel data eSIM adds a line; it does not touch the one you already "
"have. Your number, your WhatsApp account and your bank's SMS codes stay "
"exactly where they are."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1081
msgid "Which phones support eSIM?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1082
msgid ""
"iPhone XS and newer, Google Pixel 3 and newer, Samsung Galaxy S20 and newer, "
"and many recent Xiaomi, Motorola, Huawei and Oppo models. The handset also "
"has to be carrier-unlocked."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1084
msgid "Can I move an eSIM to a new phone?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1085
msgid ""
"Usually not by yourself. Most profiles can only be installed once, and "
"moving one means the seller issuing a replacement. Install it on the phone "
"you will actually travel with."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1087
msgid "Does an eSIM work without Wi-Fi?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1088
msgid ""
"Installing one needs an internet connection, which is why you install at "
"home before you fly. Once installed, it connects to the mobile network on "
"its own with no Wi-Fi involved."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1090
msgid "Do eSIMs use more battery?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1091
msgid ""
"Not meaningfully. Running two active lines uses slightly more power than "
"one, because the phone maintains two connections, but the difference is "
"small compared with screen time."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1104
msgid "Turn data roaming on for the eSIM line"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1106
msgid ""
"This is the cause more often than every other item on this page put "
"together. A travel eSIM is technically roaming on partner networks, so with "
"roaming switched off the phone shows signal bars and carries no data at all."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1109
msgid ""
"On iPhone: Settings, Mobile Service, tap the travel plan, then Mobile Data "
"Options and switch Data Roaming on. On Android: Settings, Network and "
"internet, SIMs, select the travel eSIM, then turn Roaming on."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1116
msgid "Set the eSIM as the line for mobile data"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1118
msgid ""
"Adding a second line does not automatically make it the one your phone uses "
"for data. If your home SIM is still the data line you are either getting "
"nothing or, worse, roaming charges from your own operator."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1121
msgid ""
"On iPhone: Settings, Mobile Service, Mobile Data, and choose the travel "
"plan. On Android: Settings, Network and internet, SIMs, Mobile data, and "
"select the eSIM. Leave your own SIM as the line for calls and SMS."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1128
msgid "Check the plan has actually started"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1130
msgid ""
"The clock starts on first connection at your destination, not at purchase. "
"If you are still at home, the eSIM will show as installed but will not carry "
"data, and that is correct behaviour rather than a fault."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1133
msgid ""
"Your dashboard shows the status and the data remaining once the plan is "
"live. If it says the plan has not started and you have landed, move to the "
"next step."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1139
msgid "Restart, or toggle flight mode"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1141
msgid ""
"A phone that has just landed sometimes holds on to a network registration "
"that no longer exists. Flight mode on, wait ten seconds, flight mode off is "
"the quickest version of the fix; a full restart is the thorough one."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1144
msgid ""
"Give it a minute afterwards. Registering on a foreign network is not "
"instantaneous."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1149
msgid "Select a network manually"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1151
msgid ""
"If automatic selection has latched onto an operator your plan does not use, "
"choose one of the supported operators by hand. Each destination page lists "
"which operators your eSIM works with."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1154
msgid ""
"On iPhone: Settings, Mobile Service, tap the eSIM, Network Selection, turn "
"Automatic off and pick from the list. On Android the equivalent sits under "
"SIMs, Automatically select network."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1161
msgid "Check the APN"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1163
msgid ""
"Most plans configure themselves, but some Android handsets need the access "
"point name entered by hand. The correct APN for your plan is shown on the "
"eSIM page in your dashboard and in your delivery email."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1166
msgid ""
"On Android: Settings, Network and internet, SIMs, select the eSIM, Access "
"Point Names, and add a new APN with exactly that name. iPhones almost never "
"need this."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1172
msgid "Confirm the phone is carrier-unlocked"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1174
msgid ""
"A handset locked to your home operator will install an eSIM profile and then "
"refuse to use it. If the phone came on a contract and you have never used "
"another operator's SIM in it, this is worth ruling out."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1177
msgid ""
"Your home operator can tell you the lock status and, usually, remove it. "
"There is nothing we can do from our side about a locked handset."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1183
msgid "If the QR code will not install at all"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1185
msgid ""
"Installation needs an internet connection, so do it on Wi-Fi rather than on "
"the mobile data you are trying to replace. Scan the code from another screen "
"rather than from the phone doing the installing."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1188
msgid ""
"If the code has already been used, it will not install a second time. That "
"usually means the profile is on the phone already, under a different label "
"than you expect - check the list of mobile plans in settings before "
"requesting a replacement."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1197
msgid "Signal bars but no data"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1198
msgid "Data roaming is off, or the eSIM is not set as the mobile data line."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1199
msgid "Steps 1 and 2 above, in that order."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1200
msgid "No service at all on the eSIM line"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1201
msgid ""
"The phone has not registered on a partner network yet, or the handset is "
"locked."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1202
msgid "Toggle flight mode, then try selecting a network manually."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1203
msgid "Data worked and then stopped"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1204
msgid "The bundle is used up, or the plan has expired."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1205
msgid ""
"Check the remaining data in your dashboard and buy a top-up if it is empty."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1206
msgid "Very slow speeds"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1207
msgid ""
"A congested cell, a weak indoor signal, or fair-use shaping on an unlimited "
"plan after very heavy use."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1209
msgid "Try outdoors or in another area before assuming a fault."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1210 templates/pages/support.html:50
msgid "The QR code will not scan"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1211
msgid ""
"It is being scanned from the same phone, or the profile is already installed."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1212
msgid ""
"Open the code on another screen, or check the existing plans list in "
"settings."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1213
msgid "Calls and SMS do not work"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1214
msgid "Nothing is wrong. Travel plans carry data only."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1215
msgid ""
"Use WhatsApp, FaceTime or Telegram, and keep your own SIM for traditional "
"calls."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1219
msgid "My eSIM says no service. What is the first thing to check?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1220
msgid ""
"Data roaming for the eSIM line. It has to be switched on, because a travel "
"eSIM roams on partner networks by design. This one setting accounts for most "
"reports we receive."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1222
msgid "Why do I have bars but no internet?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1223
msgid ""
"Either roaming is off for that line, or your phone is still using your home "
"SIM for mobile data. Both are two taps to fix in settings."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1225
msgid "My plan has not started counting. Is it broken?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1226
msgid ""
"Probably not. The plan begins on first connection at your destination, so "
"before you land it will sit installed and idle. That is how it is supposed "
"to work."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1228
msgid "The QR code will not install."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1229
msgid ""
"Install over Wi-Fi, scan the code from a different screen, and check whether "
"the profile is already on the phone under an unfamiliar name. If none of "
"that helps, contact support and we will reissue it."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1232
msgid "How do I know if my phone is locked?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1233
msgid ""
"Ask your home operator, or try another operator's SIM in the handset. A "
"locked phone accepts the profile and then refuses to connect with it."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1235
msgid "Nothing on this page worked."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1236
msgid ""
"Contact support with your order reference and a screenshot of the eSIM "
"settings screen. We can see the profile status from our side and will either "
"fix it or refund it."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1244
msgid "Why are your eSIM plans cheaper?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1245
msgid ""
"Two reasons, both boring. We buy wholesale data and add a thin margin rather "
"than a large one, and we do not spend money on app-install advertising, "
"which is the single biggest cost in this category. There is no trick "
"involving worse networks: travel eSIMs all ride on the same local operators."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1249
msgid "Is a cheap eSIM worse quality?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1250
msgid ""
"The network is the network. Your eSIM connects to the same national "
"operators any other seller would use, and each destination page names them. "
"What differs between sellers is the margin, not the radio."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1253
msgid "What is the cheapest way to buy data for a trip?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1254
msgid ""
"Work in price per gigabyte and per day rather than headline price, buy for "
"the trip you are actually taking, and top up if you run out. Regional plans "
"beat several country plans on any multi-country route."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1257
msgid "Are there hidden fees?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1258
msgid ""
"No. The price on the plan is the price you pay. There is no activation fee, "
"no delivery fee and nothing renews on its own."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1260
msgid "Do you run sales?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1261
msgid ""
"We would rather keep the everyday price low than run a permanent fake sale. "
"The prices on this page are simply our prices, pulled live from the "
"catalogue as you load it."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1263
msgid "Can I top up instead of buying a new eSIM?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1264
msgid ""
"Yes, and it is usually cheaper. Top-ups attach to the profile already "
"installed on your phone, so nothing is reinstalled and nothing is wasted."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1272
msgid "What does the from price mean?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1273
msgid ""
"It is the cheapest live plan for that destination, whatever its size or "
"duration. Open the destination to see the full ladder of plans with the "
"price per gigabyte and per day on each."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1275
msgid "Why do prices differ so much between countries?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1276
msgid ""
"Wholesale data costs different amounts in different markets, and we pass "
"that through rather than averaging it into one global price. Competitive "
"markets are cheap; small or remote ones are not."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1279
msgid "Are these prices in US dollars?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1280
msgid ""
"Yes, every price on the site is in USD. Your bank converts if your account "
"is in another currency."
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1282
msgid "How often do prices change?"
msgstr ""

#: apps/seo/data.py:1283
msgid ""
"They follow our wholesale costs, so they move occasionally rather than "
"daily. This table is generated from the live catalogue each time you load "
"it, so it is never out of date."
msgstr ""

