#: templates/pages/about.html:8
msgid "About"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/about.html:9
msgid "Connect without borders"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/about.html:10
msgid "The internet should follow you, not your carrier's billing department."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/about.html:13
#, python-format
msgid ""
"%(site_name)s sells prepaid travel eSIMs. We buy wholesale data from the "
"same carrier aggregators the well-known eSIM apps use, add a thin margin, "
"and pass the rest to you. That is the entire business model, and it is the "
"reason the prices look the way they do."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/about.html:15
msgid "Three kinds of freedom"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/about.html:16
msgid ""
"Freedom from the roaming bill, which is a price set by a carrier that "
"already has your card details and no reason to be kind. Freedom from carrier "
"lock-in, because a travel eSIM is a second line you own for the length of a "
"trip and nothing more. And freedom to land anywhere and already be online, "
"before the queue at passport control has moved."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/about.html:18
msgid "Why we exist"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/about.html:19
msgid ""
"Roaming is the obvious villain, but the eSIM apps that replaced it are "
"quietly expensive too. A plan that costs a few dollars wholesale routinely "
"retails for four or five times that, because the money goes into app-install "
"ads rather than into the data."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/about.html:20
msgid ""
"We took the opposite approach: no ad budget, no influencer codes, no "
"invented discount that was never a real price. The figure we strike through "
"on a plan is the going market rate for the same wholesale data elsewhere, "
"not a former price of ours. Every plan page shows the cost per gigabyte and "
"per day, so you can compare us with anyone in ten seconds."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/about.html:22
msgid "What you actually get"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/about.html:24
msgid ""
"<strong>Local networks.</strong> Your eSIM connects to real carriers at your "
"destination, not to a slow reseller pipe. We publish the partner operators "
"for every country we sell."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/about.html:25
msgid ""
"<strong>Instant delivery.</strong> The QR code appears as soon as the "
"payment clears, day or night, and lands in your inbox as well."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/about.html:26
msgid ""
"<strong>No identity checks.</strong> An email address is all we need. No "
"passport upload, no KYC, no account required to buy."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/about.html:28
msgid ""
"<strong>Crypto accepted.</strong> Pay by card if that suits you, or in "
"cryptocurrency if you would rather not hand a card number to another website."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/about.html:31
msgid ""
"<strong>Renewal is a choice.</strong> Every plan is one-off by default. Auto-"
"renewal exists for people who live abroad and want the line to stay up, and "
"you can stop it from your dashboard at any time."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/about.html:33
msgid ""
"<strong>No subscriptions.</strong> Every plan is one-off. Nothing renews "
"behind your back."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/about.html:37
msgid "How we handle your data"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/about.html:39
#, python-format
msgid ""
"We never see your traffic. What we store is what selling and supporting an "
"eSIM requires: your email, your orders, and the usage counter the network "
"reports back to us. There is no tracking pixel farm on this site. The <a "
"href=\"%(privacy_url)s\">privacy policy</a> sets out the detail, including "
"what we keep for fraud and chargeback defence."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/about.html:41
msgid "Talk to us"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/about.html:42
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Support is email, answered by the people who built this: <a href=\"mailto:"
"%(support_email)s\">%(support_email)s</a>. If an eSIM does not work, we fix "
"it or refund it."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/about.html:48 templates/seo/cheap.html:31
msgid "Wholesale in, thin margin out"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/about.html:49
msgid ""
"The price per GB is printed on every plan. Nothing is hidden behind a clever "
"label."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/about.html:53
msgid "An email is the whole signup"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/about.html:54
msgid ""
"No identity documents, no KYC, no account needed to check out as a guest."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/about.html:58
msgid "One line, many borders"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/about.html:59
msgid ""
"Regional and global plans cover a whole trip, so crossing a border does not "
"mean buying again."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/devices.html:9
msgid "Does my phone support eSIM?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/devices.html:10
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Two things have to be true: the device supports eSIM, and it is not locked "
"to another carrier. Here is how to check in ten seconds, plus the full list "
"of %(n)s supported model."
msgid_plural ""
"Two things have to be true: the device supports eSIM, and it is not locked "
"to another carrier. Here is how to check in ten seconds, plus the full list "
"of %(n)s supported models."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#: templates/pages/devices.html:10
msgid ""
"Two things have to be true: the device supports eSIM, and it is not locked "
"to another carrier. Here is how to check in ten seconds."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/devices.html:16
msgid "On iPhone"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/devices.html:17
msgid ""
"Dial <b>*#06#</b>. If an <b>EID</b> number appears, the phone supports eSIM. "
"Or open Settings, then Cellular, and look for \"Add eSIM\". iPhone XS and "
"newer, except mainland-China models."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/devices.html:21
msgid "On Android"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/devices.html:22
msgid ""
"Dial <b>*#06#</b> here too, or open Settings, then Network &amp; internet, "
"then SIMs. If you see \"Download a SIM\" or \"Add eSIM\", you are set. Pixel "
"3 and newer, Galaxy S20 and newer, plus many Xiaomi, Motorola, Oppo and "
"Huawei models."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/devices.html:26
msgid "Carrier lock"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/devices.html:27
msgid ""
"A phone locked to your home operator will refuse any other network, eSIM "
"included. Ask your operator to unlock it — usually free once the device is "
"paid off."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/devices.html:32
msgid "Full supported list"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/devices.html:38
#, python-format
msgid "%(n)s model"
msgid_plural "%(n)s models"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#: templates/pages/devices.html:49
msgid ""
"The device list is syncing from our network partner. Use the <b>*#06#</b> "
"check above in the meantime — it is the reliable answer for any phone."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/devices.html:55
msgid ""
"Regional variants are the usual exception. Some models sold in mainland "
"China ship without eSIM hardware even though the same phone supports it "
"everywhere else. If your device came from there, run the <b>*#06#</b> check "
"before you buy."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/devices.html:58
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Not sure about your exact model? Email <a class=\"link\" href=\"mailto:"
"%(support_email)s\">%(support_email)s</a> with the model number and we will "
"confirm before you buy."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/faq.html:9
msgid "Questions, answered plainly"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/faq.html:11
#, python-format
msgid ""
"If something is missing, <a class=\"link\" href=\"%(support_url)s\">ask us</"
"a> — we answer by email, usually within a couple of hours."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/faq.html:18
msgid "Still stuck?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/faq.html:19
msgid ""
"Tell us the order reference and what your phone is showing. Real people read "
"it, and an eSIM that cannot connect gets fixed or refunded."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/faq.html:21 templates/seo/not_working.html:95
#: templates/seo/payment_method.html:48
msgid "Contact support"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/how_it_works.html:8
msgid "The basics"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/how_it_works.html:9 templates/seo/what_is_esim.html:25
msgid "How an eSIM actually works"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/how_it_works.html:10
msgid ""
"No plastic, no shop, no roaming surcharge. Here is the whole thing in four "
"steps and about two minutes of your time."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/how_it_works.html:21 templates/seo/what_is_esim.html:9
msgid "What is an eSIM?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/how_it_works.html:22
msgid ""
"A chip already soldered into your phone that can hold a mobile plan "
"downloaded over the internet. The QR code you scan is just the download "
"instruction."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/how_it_works.html:26
msgid "Two lines at once"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/how_it_works.html:27
msgid ""
"Your normal SIM keeps handling calls, SMS and WhatsApp on your own number. "
"The eSIM only carries data, so nothing about your identity changes."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/how_it_works.html:31
msgid "When the clock starts"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/how_it_works.html:32
msgid ""
"On first connection at your destination — not at purchase, not at install. "
"Install at home on Wi-Fi and nothing is wasted."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/how_it_works.html:38
msgid ""
"<b>One setting people forget.</b> Turn <b>Data Roaming ON</b> for the eSIM "
"line. It sounds wrong, but a travel eSIM is technically roaming on partner "
"networks — with the setting off it will show bars and carry no data."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/how_it_works.html:44
msgid "Local networks, not a reseller pipe"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/how_it_works.html:45
msgid ""
"The profile registers on real carriers at your destination, the same ones a "
"local pay-as-you-go SIM would use. Each destination page lists the partner "
"operators."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/how_it_works.html:49
msgid "One profile, one device"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/how_it_works.html:50
msgid ""
"An eSIM installs on a single phone and cannot be moved afterwards, so "
"install it on the device you are travelling with. The QR code stays in your "
"account either way."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/how_it_works.html:54
msgid "Running low? Top up"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/how_it_works.html:55
msgid ""
"Add data to the line you already installed from your dashboard. No new QR "
"code, no reinstall, no second profile cluttering your settings."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/how_it_works.html:63
msgid "Questions people ask first"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:7
msgid "Privacy Policy"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:9 templates/pages/refund.html:9
#: templates/pages/terms.html:9
#, python-format
msgid "Last updated %(updated)s"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:11
#, python-format
msgid ""
"This policy explains what %(site_name)s collects, why, and what we never "
"touch. The short version: we need an email address to deliver an eSIM, we "
"keep enough of a record to defend a payment dispute, and we do not look at "
"your traffic."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:13
msgid "What we collect"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:15
msgid ""
"<strong>Your email address.</strong> Required — it is how the QR code and "
"receipt reach you."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:16
msgid ""
"<strong>Order records.</strong> Which plan you bought, when, the subtotal, "
"any discount applied, the amount actually charged, and the reference from "
"the payment provider."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:17
msgid ""
"<strong>eSIM technical data.</strong> The ICCID we issued you, its "
"activation status, the data counter the network reports, and the radio "
"technology last seen. This comes from our connectivity partner, not from "
"your device."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:18
msgid ""
"<strong>Request details attached to an order.</strong> The IP address the "
"order was placed from, the browser user agent, the browser language and the "
"referring page. See the fraud-prevention section below."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:19
msgid ""
"<strong>Coupon and discount records.</strong> The code you entered, the "
"order it applied to and the discount amount."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:20
msgid ""
"<strong>Subscription records</strong>, if you choose an auto-renewing plan: "
"the billing identifiers our payment processor gives us, the price per cycle, "
"the renewal date and the renewal history."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:21
msgid ""
"<strong>Support and assistant conversations</strong>, including anything you "
"type into the chat assistant."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:22
msgid ""
"<strong>Optional profile data.</strong> A display name, if you enter one, "
"and a name you give an eSIM line to tell it from another."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:25
msgid "What we never collect"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:27
msgid ""
"The content of your traffic — the sites you visit, your messages, your "
"calls. We are a reseller of connectivity, and none of that reaches us."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:28
msgid ""
"Card numbers. Card payments are handled entirely by Stripe; we receive only "
"a token and the outcome."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:29
msgid "Identity documents. There is no KYC, no passport upload, no ID check."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:30
msgid ""
"Location beyond the country of the network your eSIM registers on, which is "
"simply the destination you bought."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:33
msgid "Fraud prevention and chargeback defence"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:34
msgid ""
"Digital goods delivered in seconds are a standard target for stolen cards, "
"and a guest order has no account behind it. So, when an order is placed, we "
"record the IP address the request came from, the browser user agent string, "
"the browser language and the referring page, and we store them against that "
"order."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:35
msgid ""
"We use that record for three things and nothing else: to score an order for "
"payment fraud before we provision a line, to answer a bank or card scheme "
"when a payment is disputed, and to trace abuse of coupons or of the network "
"itself. It is never used for advertising, profiling or tracking you across "
"other sites, and we do not sell or share it for those purposes."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:36
msgid ""
"The lawful basis is our legitimate interest in preventing fraud and in "
"defending payment disputes, and, where card-scheme rules require it, our "
"legal obligation. We keep this request data for 24 months from the order "
"date and then delete it, which leaves a margin over the dispute windows the "
"card schemes allow. The order itself, minus that request data, is kept for "
"as long as accounting law requires."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:38
msgid "Coupons and promotions"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:39
msgid ""
"If you use a discount code we store the code, the order it was applied to "
"and the amount it took off. Where a code is limited to one use per customer, "
"we also keep a redemption record linked to your email address or account so "
"the limit can be enforced."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:40
msgid ""
"This is part of processing your order, and the record stays with the order "
"for the same period. Discount codes are not used to build a marketing "
"profile, and entering one does not sign you up to anything."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:43
msgid "Auto-renewing subscriptions"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:44
msgid ""
"A subscription needs an account, because a recurring charge needs somewhere "
"you can see and stop it. For each subscription we store the customer and "
"subscription identifiers our payment processor returns, the price per cycle, "
"the renewal interval, the date of the next renewal, how many times it has "
"renewed and whether it is set to cancel at the end of the period. The card "
"itself stays with the payment processor."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:45
#, python-format
msgid ""
"We process this to perform the contract you entered into. You can cancel at "
"any time from your dashboard or from the billing portal; cancelling stops "
"future renewals and does not refund the period already delivered. The full "
"commercial terms are in the <a href=\"%(terms_url)s\">terms of service</a> "
"and the <a href=\"%(refund_url)s\">refund policy</a>. After a subscription "
"ends, the billing record is kept for accounting."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:47
msgid "The chat assistant"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:48
msgid ""
"The assistant in your account is an AI model answering support questions "
"with the context of your own orders and eSIM lines. Conversations are stored "
"against your account so the thread makes sense next time you open it, and so "
"a human can pick it up where the model left off."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:49
msgid ""
"Our support team can read those conversations. We review them to resolve "
"escalations, to check answer quality and to catch abuse. Messages are sent "
"to our AI provider, Anthropic, to generate a reply; under their commercial "
"terms they are not used to train their models."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:50
msgid ""
"Please do not paste passwords, full card numbers, recovery codes or identity "
"documents into the chat. We never ask for any of them, and the assistant "
"does not need them to help you. If you post something sensitive by accident, "
"email us and we will delete that conversation."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:51
msgid ""
"Assistant conversations are kept while your account is open and are deleted "
"with it, or sooner on request."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:53
msgid "Why we process it"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:54
msgid ""
"To sell and deliver the eSIM you asked for and to run any subscription you "
"started (contract), to keep records for accounting and to prevent and "
"investigate fraud (legal obligation and legitimate interest), and — only if "
"you opt in — to send occasional product emails (consent). Transactional "
"emails about your own orders are sent regardless of marketing preferences, "
"because you need them."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:56
msgid "Who we share it with"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:58
msgid ""
"<strong>Our connectivity partner</strong>, to issue and manage the eSIM. "
"They receive your email address and the plan you bought."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:59
msgid ""
"<strong>Stripe</strong> and <strong>NOWPayments</strong>, to take payment "
"and, for subscriptions, to bill each renewal."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:60
msgid ""
"<strong>Anthropic</strong>, to generate chat assistant replies, where the "
"assistant is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:61
msgid ""
"<strong>Our email provider</strong>, to deliver order and support email."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:62
msgid ""
"<strong>Our hosting and error-monitoring providers</strong>, which process "
"data incidentally while running the site."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:63
msgid ""
"A bank, card scheme or payment processor investigating a disputed payment, "
"limited to the evidence that dispute requires."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:65
msgid "We do not sell personal data, and we do not share it with advertisers."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:67
msgid "Cookies and analytics"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:68
msgid ""
"We set a session cookie so the site can keep you signed in and remember a "
"guest order, a CSRF cookie that protects forms, and a cookie recording your "
"chosen language. Your light or dark mode preference is not a cookie at all: "
"it is stored in your own browser and never sent to us. If analytics is "
"enabled, it runs with advertising signals switched off and IP anonymisation "
"on."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:70
msgid "How long we keep it"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:72
msgid ""
"Order, payment, coupon and subscription billing records: as long as "
"accounting law requires."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:73
msgid ""
"IP address, user agent, browser language and referrer attached to an order: "
"24 months from the order date."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:74
msgid ""
"eSIM technical records: while the line is live and for a short period "
"afterwards for support."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:75
msgid ""
"Support tickets and assistant conversations: while your account is open, or "
"sooner on request."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:77
msgid ""
"If you delete your account we deactivate it and unlink your email; records "
"we are required to keep for accounting remain, and are not used for anything "
"else."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:79
msgid "Your rights"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:80
#, python-format
msgid ""
"You can ask for a copy of your data, correction, deletion, or an export, and "
"you can object to processing based on legitimate interest, including the "
"fraud record described above — though we may need to keep it where a payment "
"dispute is open. You can withdraw marketing consent at any time from the "
"unsubscribe link or your account page. Email <a href=\"mailto:"
"%(support_email)s\">%(support_email)s</a> and we will action it. You also "
"have the right to complain to your local data protection authority."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:82
msgid "Changes and contact"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/privacy.html:83
msgid ""
"We may update this policy. The version in force is the one published here, "
"and material changes are reflected in the date at the top of this page."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:7
msgid "Refund Policy"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:12
msgid ""
"eSIM plans are delivered instantly and digitally, so the rules are simple "
"and we apply them consistently."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:14
msgid "Full refund"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:15
msgid "You get your money back in full when:"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:17
msgid ""
"the eSIM has <strong>not been installed</strong> on a device and has no "
"usage, and you ask within <strong>24 hours</strong> of purchase; or"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:18
msgid "we failed to deliver the profile (a provisioning error on our side); or"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:19
msgid ""
"the eSIM cannot connect at your destination and our support team cannot fix "
"it — we check the line's own network log before deciding, so you do not have "
"to prove anything."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:22
msgid "No refund"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:24
msgid ""
"The profile has been installed and has used data. An installed profile "
"cannot be reissued or resold, so its cost is already spent."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:25
msgid ""
"The validity period expired with data unused. Unused days and gigabytes have "
"no cash value."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:26
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Your device turned out to be locked to another carrier or does not support "
"eSIM. Please check our <a href=\"%(devices_url)s\">compatibility page</a> "
"before buying — ask us if you are unsure and we will confirm for your exact "
"model."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:27
msgid "You bought the wrong destination and had already installed the profile."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:28
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Loss caused by breach of our <a href=\"%(terms_url)s\">acceptable use rules</"
"a>."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:31 templates/partials/dash_tabs.html:5
#: templates/partials/header.html:84 templates/subscriptions/list.html:9
msgid "Subscriptions"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:32
msgid ""
"A subscription is refunded on the same principles as a one-off plan, applied "
"one billing period at a time. Cancel before a renewal and you are not "
"charged for it: cancelling from your dashboard or the billing portal takes "
"effect at the end of the period you are in, and no further payment is taken."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:33
msgid ""
"A period that has already renewed and been delivered is not refundable once "
"the data has been added to your line and used, in the same way an installed "
"one-off plan is not. Cancelling mid-period does not produce a pro-rata "
"refund; your data and days stay usable until the period ends."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:34
msgid ""
"There are two exceptions, and we apply them without argument. If a renewal "
"was charged and the data was never added to your line, we refund that period "
"in full. If you cancelled and a renewal was taken anyway, we refund it in "
"full — tell us and we will not ask you to prove it."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:35
msgid ""
"The first period of a subscription follows the ordinary rules above: "
"uninstalled and unused within 24 hours, and it is refunded in full."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:37
msgid "Orders with a discount code"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:38
msgid ""
"A refund returns the amount you actually paid — the discounted total shown "
"on your order, not the price before the discount. A discount code has no "
"cash value of its own and is never refunded as money."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:39
msgid ""
"Where a refund is partial, it is calculated from the amount paid. A code "
"used on a refunded order is treated as spent and does not automatically "
"become available again; if the refund was our fault, ask us and we will "
"reissue it."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:41
msgid "How to request one"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:42
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Email <a href=\"mailto:%(support_email)s\">%(support_email)s</a> with your "
"order reference (ES-XXXXXXX). We answer within one business day and, when a "
"refund is due, issue it to the original payment method."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:44
msgid "Card and crypto refunds"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:45
msgid ""
"Card refunds go back through Stripe and typically appear within 5-10 "
"business days depending on your bank. Cryptocurrency refunds are sent to a "
"wallet address you provide, in the same coin, at the amount received; "
"network fees are deducted, and exchange-rate movement between payment and "
"refund is not compensated."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:47
msgid "Partial refunds"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:48
msgid ""
"If a plan worked for part of its period and then failed because of a network "
"problem on our side, we refund pro rata for the unused days once support has "
"confirmed the fault."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:50
msgid "Chargebacks"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/refund.html:51
msgid ""
"Please talk to us before opening a dispute — an email is faster than a "
"chargeback, and we would rather fix the problem. Accounts used for "
"chargeback abuse are suspended."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:11
msgid "Something not working? Let us fix it."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:12
msgid ""
"Nearly every fault is one setting on the phone. Try the quick checks below "
"first — if\n"
"        none of them apply, open a ticket and we answer by email. You do not "
"need an account."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:20
msgid "Bars, but no internet"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:21
msgid ""
"Turn <b>Data Roaming ON</b> for the eSIM line, then set that line as the "
"one\n"
"          used for mobile data. This is the fix roughly nine times out of "
"ten."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:26
msgid "Data is using the wrong line"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:27
msgid ""
"Your home SIM stays active on purpose, so calls and bank codes keep "
"working.\n"
"          Check that mobile data is pointed at the eSIM and not at your home "
"line."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:32
msgid "No service or not registered"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:33
msgid ""
"Toggle flight mode, restart the phone once, then pick the carrier by hand "
"in\n"
"          network settings. The profile registers on the next boot."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:38
msgid "Data or days ran out"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:39
msgid ""
"Validity starts on the first connection at your destination, not at "
"purchase.\n"
"          Top up from the dashboard and the data attaches to the same eSIM."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:44
msgid "The phone is carrier-locked"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:45
msgid ""
"A locked phone refuses any other network, eSIM included. Your carrier "
"unlocks\n"
"          it, usually free once the contract is paid off."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:51
msgid ""
"Scan it from another screen, or use manual entry with the activation details "
"on\n"
"          your eSIM page. One profile installs on one device only."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:58
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Step-by-step install guides live on the <a class=\"link\" "
"href=\"%(how_url)s\">how it works</a>\n"
"      and <a class=\"link\" href=\"%(faq_url)s\">FAQ</a> pages."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:68
msgid "Your tickets"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:69 templates/partials/header.html:79
msgid "Signed in as"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:75
msgid "Reference"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:76 templates/pages/support.html:128
msgid "Subject"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:78
msgid "Last activity"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:105
msgid "Open a ticket"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:106
msgid ""
"Give us the order reference or the ICCID and we can look at the real line\n"
"          instead of guessing. You get a reference back and we reply by "
"email."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:113
msgid "Your email"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:115
msgid "The address you bought with"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:116
msgid ""
"Use the address from your order so we can match it. We email you a private "
"link to the thread."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:121
msgid "What is this about?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:134
msgid "Order reference"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:138
msgid "ICCID (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:144
msgid "What is happening?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:146
msgid "Phone model, which country you are in, and what the screen says."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:149
msgid "Send message"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/support.html:156 templates/partials/assistant_widget.html:14
msgid "Chat with the assistant"
msgstr ""

