#: templates/pages/terms.html:7
msgid "Terms of Service"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:12
#, python-format
msgid ""
"These terms govern your use of %(site_name)s and the prepaid mobile data "
"plans (\"eSIM plans\") sold through it. By buying or using a plan you accept "
"them."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:14
msgid "1. What we sell"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:15
msgid ""
"We resell prepaid mobile data delivered as an eSIM profile. Plans are "
"<strong>data only</strong>: they do not include GSM voice calls or SMS. You "
"can make calls and send messages over the data connection using apps such as "
"WhatsApp, FaceTime or Telegram."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:16
msgid ""
"Coverage, available radio technology (4G/5G) and speed depend on the local "
"carriers at your destination and on your device. We publish the partner "
"operators for each destination, but we cannot guarantee a specific operator, "
"a specific speed, or coverage in every location."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:18
msgid "2. Validity and activation"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:19
msgid ""
"A plan's validity period starts when the eSIM first connects to a mobile "
"network in a covered country, not when you buy or install it. Once started, "
"the period runs continuously in calendar days and cannot be paused. Unused "
"data and unused days expire at the end of the period and are not refundable "
"or transferable."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:21
msgid "3. Your device"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:22
#, python-format
msgid ""
"You are responsible for checking that your device supports eSIM and is not "
"locked to another carrier before buying. Our <a "
"href=\"%(devices_url)s\">compatibility page</a> lists supported models. An "
"eSIM profile can normally be installed on only one device and cannot be "
"moved afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:24
msgid "4. Prices and payment"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:25
msgid ""
"Prices are shown in US dollars and include our margin. Payment is taken at "
"checkout by card (through Stripe) or in cryptocurrency (through "
"NOWPayments). Crypto payments are credited at the amount actually received; "
"if less than the invoice arrives, nothing is provisioned until the "
"difference is paid or the payment is refunded."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:26
msgid ""
"Where a plan shows a comparison figure next to the price, that figure is the "
"going market rate charged elsewhere for equivalent wholesale data, not a "
"previous price of ours. It is there so you can judge the saving, and it is "
"not an offer by us at that amount."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:28
msgid "5. Coupons and promotional discounts"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:29
msgid ""
"We sometimes issue discount codes. A code is valid only for what it says: it "
"may be limited to certain plans, destinations or minimum order values, may "
"expire, may be capped in total redemptions, and may be limited to one use "
"per customer. The discount is applied at checkout and shown on the order "
"before you pay; if no discount appears, the code did not apply and the full "
"price stands."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:30
msgid ""
"Codes have no cash value, cannot be exchanged for money, cannot be applied "
"to an order that is already placed, and cannot normally be combined with "
"another code. We may withdraw a code at any time, and we may cancel a "
"discount or an order where a code has been obtained or used abusively, for "
"example by creating accounts to reuse a one-per-customer offer."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:32
msgid "6. Delivery"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:33
msgid ""
"eSIM profiles are delivered electronically, immediately after payment "
"clears, to the email address you enter at checkout and to your account if "
"you have one. It is your responsibility to enter a working email address. If "
"a provisioning failure occurs on our side, we either deliver the plan or "
"refund it in full."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:35
msgid "7. Auto-renewing subscriptions"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:36
msgid ""
"Most plans are one-off purchases and nothing renews. Where a plan is offered "
"as a subscription, this is stated clearly before you pay, and buying it "
"starts a recurring payment. A subscription requires an account, because a "
"recurring charge needs somewhere you can manage and stop it."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:37
msgid ""
"A subscription renews automatically at the end of each billing period, at "
"the interval shown when you subscribed, and charges the payment method held "
"by our processor at the price shown for that plan. Each renewal tops up the "
"same eSIM line, so you do not reinstall a profile. Your dashboard shows the "
"renewal date before it happens."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:38
msgid ""
"You can cancel at any time from your dashboard or from the billing portal. "
"Cancelling stops all future renewals; it does not refund the period you are "
"already in, and the data and days of that period remain yours until they "
"expire. Access continues to the end of the period you have paid for."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:39
msgid ""
"If a renewal payment fails, the subscription is marked as needing attention "
"and we may retry through our payment processor. If it cannot be collected, "
"the subscription stops and no further data is added to the line. We may "
"change subscription pricing, but only with notice before a renewal, and you "
"can cancel before that renewal if you do not accept it."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:41
msgid "8. Refunds"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:42
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Refund terms are set out in our <a href=\"%(refund_url)s\">refund policy</"
"a>, which forms part of these terms."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:44
msgid "9. Acceptable use"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:45
msgid ""
"You may not use our plans to send spam, to run automated abuse against third "
"parties, for unlawful activity, or to resell the connection commercially "
"without our written agreement. Unlimited plans are for normal personal use: "
"local networks may shape extreme continuous consumption, in particular "
"sustained tethering, under their fair-use rules."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:46
msgid ""
"We may suspend a line that is being used in breach of this section, without "
"refund."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:48
msgid "10. The chat assistant"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:49
msgid ""
"Signed-in customers can use an AI assistant for support questions. It "
"answers from our documentation and from your own order and eSIM data, and it "
"can hand the conversation to a human. It is a support tool, not advice: "
"where an answer from the assistant conflicts with these terms, the refund "
"policy or the plan details on the product page, those documents govern."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:50
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Conversations are stored on your account, can be read by our support team, "
"and are sent to our AI provider to generate replies. Do not paste passwords, "
"full card numbers, recovery codes or identity documents into the chat — we "
"will never ask for them. The <a href=\"%(privacy_url)s\">privacy policy</a> "
"explains how these conversations are handled. We may limit or withdraw "
"access to the assistant if it is abused."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:52
msgid "11. Liability"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:53
msgid ""
"We provide the connectivity service with reasonable care but do not warrant "
"uninterrupted or error-free service. To the extent permitted by law our "
"total liability for any claim relating to a plan is limited to the amount "
"you paid for that plan. We are not liable for indirect or consequential "
"loss, including missed bookings, lost work or data charges incurred on "
"another network."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:55
msgid "12. Accounts"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:56
msgid ""
"You may buy as a guest or create an account; a subscription requires an "
"account. Keep your credentials safe; you are responsible for activity under "
"your account. We may suspend accounts used fraudulently, including for "
"payment fraud, coupon abuse or chargeback abuse."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:57
#, python-format
msgid ""
"We record the IP address, browser user agent, browser language and referring "
"page of each order for fraud prevention and to defend payment disputes, as "
"described in the <a href=\"%(privacy_url)s\">privacy policy</a>."
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:59
msgid "13. Changes"
msgstr ""

#: templates/pages/terms.html:60
msgid ""
"We may update these terms. The version in force is the one published here "
"when you buy. For a subscription, the version in force is the one published "
"when the current period began, and material changes are notified before the "
"next renewal. Material changes are noted by the date at the top of this page."
msgstr ""

