#: templates/seo/what_is_esim.html:8
msgid "eSIM explained"
msgstr ""

#: templates/seo/what_is_esim.html:10
msgid ""
"An eSIM is a SIM card that is already inside your phone. Instead of "
"collecting a piece of plastic from a shop, you scan a QR code and the mobile "
"plan downloads onto a chip that was soldered in at the factory. Everything "
"else about it behaves like a SIM, because it is one."
msgstr ""

#: templates/seo/what_is_esim.html:16
#, python-format
msgid "Try one from $%(p)s"
msgstr ""

#: templates/seo/what_is_esim.html:17
msgid "Check your phone"
msgstr ""

#: templates/seo/what_is_esim.html:26
msgid ""
"A physical SIM is a small computer with a number on it. It stores the "
"credentials that tell a mobile network who you are and which plan you have "
"paid for. An eSIM stores exactly the same credentials, but it is a permanent "
"chip inside the handset that can be written to over the internet rather than "
"a card you swap."
msgstr ""

#: templates/seo/what_is_esim.html:32
msgid ""
"The QR code you scan is not the plan itself. It is an address and an "
"activation token: your phone reads it, connects to the provisioning server "
"it points at, downloads the profile and installs it. That is why installing "
"an eSIM needs an internet connection and why you should do it on Wi-Fi at "
"home rather than after you land."
msgstr ""

#: templates/seo/what_is_esim.html:38
msgid ""
"Once installed, the profile sits in your phone's settings next to your "
"existing line. You can turn it on and off, choose which line carries mobile "
"data, and delete it when the trip is over. Most modern phones can store "
"several profiles and keep two of them active at the same time."
msgstr ""

#: templates/seo/what_is_esim.html:45
msgid ""
"They are related, and the two terms get muddled constantly. Dual SIM "
"describes a phone that can run two lines at once. An eSIM is one way of "
"supplying one of those lines. Most recent phones are dual SIM precisely "
"because they pair one physical tray with an eSIM, and some newer models "
"support two eSIM profiles active together with no tray at all."
msgstr ""

#: templates/seo/what_is_esim.html:51
msgid ""
"For a traveller this is the whole point. Your normal SIM stays where it is "
"and keeps your number reachable for calls, SMS and the bank codes that "
"follow you everywhere. The travel eSIM carries the data. Nothing about your "
"identity, your WhatsApp account or your contacts changes."
msgstr ""

#: templates/seo/what_is_esim.html:57
msgid "What an eSIM is not"
msgstr ""

#: templates/seo/what_is_esim.html:58
msgid ""
"It is not a VPN and it does not hide anything. It is not a second phone "
"number unless you specifically buy a plan that includes one; travel data "
"plans are data-only, which is why calls go over WhatsApp, FaceTime or "
"Telegram. And it is not tied to a country: the same chip in your phone can "
"hold a plan from anywhere."
msgstr ""

#: templates/seo/what_is_esim.html:70
msgid "eSIM vs physical SIM"
msgstr ""

#: templates/seo/what_is_esim.html:71
msgid ""
"The differences that actually change what you do, rather than the ones that "
"only matter to network engineers."
msgstr ""

#: templates/seo/what_is_esim.html:77
msgid "Aspect"
msgstr ""

#: templates/seo/what_is_esim.html:79
msgid "Physical SIM"
msgstr ""

#: templates/seo/what_is_esim.html:93
msgid ""
"The one real disadvantage: an eSIM needs a reasonably recent, carrier-"
"unlocked handset, and most profiles cannot be moved to a different phone "
"once installed."
msgstr ""

#: templates/seo/what_is_esim.html:100
msgid "Getting one onto your phone"
msgstr ""

#: templates/seo/what_is_esim.html:101
msgid "Four steps, about two minutes, no shop involved."
msgstr ""

#: templates/seo/what_is_esim.html:107
